        "status": "static_source_finding_plus_analytical_bound",
        "description": "ProcessCommand() parses a 16-bit pulse field and passes it directly to TurnBody()/MoveForward() without clamping. The finite-pulse boundedness therefore comes from the host-side clamp (max 25 body pulses in the audited runtime), not from the MCU execution boundary. Because the seven-byte frame has neither a sequence number nor a CRC, a corrupted pulse field is not detected by the controller.",
